{
  "_comment": [
    "The lpsd service definition: what peinit starts, and when.",
    "",
    "Requires authd, and the direction is deliberate. Sources dial in to the",
    "authority over /run/psi.sock, so the authority has to be listening first.",
    "That inverts the more obvious 'the authority depends on its backend', and",
    "the ordering guarantee moves here rather than being lost -- which is why",
    "authd does not gate its own readiness on sources having registered. peinit",
    "already owns dependency ordering; authd re-implementing it would be a",
    "second, worse copy.",
    "",
    "Readiness is Notify (0), and what its READY=1 *means* is the load-bearing",
    "part: lpsd signals ready once authd has ACKNOWLEDGED its registration, not",
    "merely once its process exists. So anything ordered after lpsd -- login,",
    "above all -- finds a system that can actually authenticate, rather than one",
    "that will fail every attempt with AuthorityUnavailable during the window",
    "before registration completes.",
    "",
    "RuntimeDirectories names lpsd, because its admin socket lives in a",
    "subdirectory (/run/lpsd/admin.sock, unlike authd's three, which sit",
    "directly in /run). peinit creates it with a proper Peios descriptor --",
    "SYSTEM, Administrators and lpsd's own service SID -- rather than whatever",
    "lpsd's umask would produce. lpsd still creates the directory itself if it",
    "is absent, so this is the descriptor rather than the directory.",
    "",
    "It does not cover /var/state/lpsd, which lpsd also creates:",
    "RuntimeDirectories only makes paths under /run.",
    "",
    "ErrorControl is Critical (1), for authd's reason one step along: a boot",
    "with an authority but no principal source can present a prompt and never",
    "satisfy it.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the lpsd package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an image",
    "names it in [registry] autoapply. Registering lpsd *with authd* is a",
    "separate seed (lpsd-authd-registration.reg) and a separate decision."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\lpsd",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath",          "type": "sz",    "data": "/sbin/lpsd" },
        { "name": "Triggers",           "type": "multi", "data": ["boot"] },
        { "name": "RuntimeDirectories", "type": "multi", "data": ["lpsd"] },
        { "name": "Requires",           "type": "multi", "data": ["authd"] },
        { "name": "Identity",           "type": "sz",    "data": "SYSTEM" },
        { "name": "Readiness",          "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy",      "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl",       "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "DisplayName",        "type": "sz",    "data": "Local principal source" },
        { "name": "Description",        "type": "sz",    "data": "Local identity database and the local half of PSI" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
